facts:
A parabola is a smooth, **symmetrical** U-shape with exactly **one turning point**.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6.2cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-2.8,xmax=4.8,ymin=-3.4,ymax=7,xtick=\empty,ytick=\empty,clip=false,xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[dashed,gray] coordinates {(1,-3.2) (1,6.6)};
\addplot[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.74:3.74,samples=80]{1.2*(x-1)*(x-1)-2};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,mark size=2pt,black] coordinates {(1,-2)};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (axis cs:0.6,3.4) {line of symmetry};
\node[below right,font=\small] at (axis cs:1.15,-2.15) {turning point};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

It has no turning point, growing or decaying one way and flattening towards a horizontal line it never reaches.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6.4cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-3.4,xmax=3.4,ymin=-3,ymax=9.6,xtick=\empty,ytick=\empty,clip=false,xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=-3.4:2.05,samples=60]{exp(x*ln(3))};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (axis cs:-2.3,-0.8) -- (axis cs:-2.95,-0.1);
\node[font=\small,align=center,anchor=north] at (axis cs:-1.7,-1) {never reaches\\ the $x$-axis};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

