Is this graph a parabola or an exponential curve? Give one reason.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,<->] (-3,0)--(3,0);
\draw[black,<->] (0,-2)--(0,5);
\path (3,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-2.3:2.3,samples=80] plot (\x,{(\x)*(\x)-1});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Is this graph a parabola or an exponential curve? Give one reason.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curvered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,<->] (-3,0)--(3,0);
\draw[black,<->] (0,-1)--(0,5);
\path (3,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curvered,thick,<->,domain=-2.2:3,samples=80] plot (\x,{exp(-\x*ln(2))});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

